From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:40:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: report the RSS hash function

Since the ethtool_rxfh_param API, rxfh->hfunc is an output the core
zeroes before calling .get_rxfh, so "if (rxfh->hfunc)" (left from the
old u8 *hfunc pointer argument) never set it, and ethtool -x showed no
hash function. Always report Toeplitz.

[From pesa1234's tree (999-9903, which has no author line), ported to
 OpenWrt 6.12 for MilkFlint unchanged.]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
index 3ec4cd5..6060cfe 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -5424,8 +5424,7 @@ static int mtk_get_rxfh(struct net_device *dev, struct ethtool_rxfh_param *rxfh)
 	if (!MTK_HAS_CAPS(eth->soc->caps, MTK_RSS) || !eth->soc->rss_num)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
-	if (rxfh->hfunc)
-		rxfh->hfunc = ETH_RSS_HASH_TOP;	/* Toeplitz */
+	rxfh->hfunc = ETH_RSS_HASH_TOP;	/* Toeplitz */
 
 	if (rxfh->key)
 		memcpy(rxfh->key, rss_params->hash_key,
